    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §4, Chap 374 of 2014",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5323\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 374 of the laws of 2014 amend-\ning the education law relating to the leasing of real property by boards\nof cooperative education services, in relation to extending the effec-\ntiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the possibility for Boards of Cooperative Educational Services\n(BOCES) to enter into leases with non-public entities not to exceed\ntwenty years until July 1, 2024.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 4 of chapter 374 of the laws of 2014, which\nallows BOCES to enter into leases not to exceed ten years with public\nentities and not to exceed twenty years if the lease is with a non-publ-\nic entity, by providing that the act shall be deemed repealed on July 1,\n2024.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPrior to the enactment of Chapter 374 of the Laws of 2014, Boards of\nCooperative Educational Services (BOCES) were limited to leases with a\nmaximum duration of ten years. Based on the enactment of Chapter 374 of\nthe Laws of 2014, BOCES are now authorized to enter into 20-year leases.\nAs a result, they are able to better plan future projects, save costs,\nand provide greater efficiencies to the overall operations of the BOCES\ndistrict. This authorization is scheduled to expire on July 1, 2019.\nBecause this law has been successful in helping BOCES achieve greater\nefficiencies and save costs, it should be extended to July 1, 2024.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
